{
  "id": "COMPOUND:41593 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound in question and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that are themselves targets of this enzyme. The compound is directly linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is in turn targeted by several other molecules, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, and (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. These molecules are all known to interact with the SDR family, indicating a potential pathway where the compound may act as a substrate or inhibitor of the enzyme. The consistent targeting of the SDR family member 9 by multiple compounds suggests a functional role in the metabolic pathway, possibly in the context of sialylation or other enzymatic processes. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound may influence the activity of the SDR family, potentially through direct interaction or by modulating the activity of its targets.",
